Plates were read using an iSpot Spectrum Analyzer (AID) and results are reported as spot forming units (SFU) per million cells based on the means of technical triplicates. Background responses from irrelevant control peptide restimulations were subtracted from results. To determine whether an individual patient’s on-treatment change in IFNγ SFU responses represents a true increase from baseline, we first calculated the repeatability coefficient (RC)61. The RC was defined as:\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
