                                                  \setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
                                                  \begin{document}$$({Maximal}\,{Absolute}\,{Change}-{RC},{Maximal}\,{Absolute}\,{Change}+{RC})$$\end{document}(MaximalAbsoluteChange−RC,MaximalAbsoluteChange+RC)If the 95% CI did not include 0, the patient’s change was considered a true increase beyond baseline variability rather than due to chance.

